//
// Phi-4-mini Q4NX verify gate: top-k token-level inclusion check, NPU q4nx vs
// HF bf16, 2 prompts × 32 greedy tokens, k=5 (use `make verify-full` for the
// full sweep locally). Exercises the full production prefill + decode path
// through the verify subsystem (verify/verify_runner.py); NPU weights come from
// the FastFlowLM model.q4nx bundle, the reference from the HF bf16 checkpoint.
//
// Skips cleanly when HF_TOKEN is unset (reference + tokenizer downloads need it).
//
// `make compile-decode` is mandatory here, not an optimization: every model emits
// the same decode_L<N>.* names into the shared fused_decode dir, so without it this
// test would consume whichever model's templates ran last (phi4_mini_q4nx sorts
// first). It is idempotent per MODEL_TYPE, hence llvm_link_pre23 below.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, llvm_link_pre23, hf_token, hfweights_microsoft_phi_4_mini_instruct, hfweights_fastflowlm_phi4_mini_instruct_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_verify
// RUN: cd test_peano_verify
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile-decode PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// Q4NX_VERIFY_FORCE_PREFILL=1 exercises the production prefill -> KV-handoff ->
// decode path. Without it these short prompts are replayed through the decode,
// whose LM head is the 4-bit cascade rather than the prefill's bf16 head -- see
// README 'Two LM-head precisions'.
// RUN: env Q4NX_VERIFY_FORCE_PREFILL=1 make -f %S/Makefile verify PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: [verify] PASS
